      "content": "1200mg of ibuprofen is a lot, but if you're in severe pain, you can take it. Just make sure to take it with food to avoid stomach upset. As for the antibiotics, I'd recommend sticking to the ones prescribed by your surgeon. Taking leftover antibiotics from a previous infection isn't a good idea. It could lead to antibiotic resistance or other complications. Stick to the plan, and you'll be fine. Remember, I'm here to help you through this!",
